# Frontend — Vanilla Web

## Project Structure
```
features/<name>/   # co-located .js, .css, .test.js
shared/api/        # shared fetch helpers
shared/utils/
assets/scripts/    # entry point (e.g. main.js)
```

## HTML
- Semantic elements (`<nav>`, `<main>`, `<article>`, `<button>`, not `<div onclick>`)
- Forms: associated `<label>`, appropriate `type`, `required`, `autocomplete`
- ARIA only when native semantics are insufficient
- Progressive enhancement: core functionality works without JavaScript

## JavaScript — Modules & DOM
- Entry point initializes features: `document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init)`
- `init(root)` enriches existing DOM and returns a teardown function when listeners are attached
- `create(...)` builds an element or API and returns `{ element, destroy }`
- Select via `data-*` attributes, not classes meant for styling
- Prefer event delegation on stable parent elements
- Remove event listeners on teardown when dynamically mounting/unmounting
- Batch DOM reads/writes; use `DocumentFragment` for multiple insertions
- Never attach state to `window`; encapsulate in module closures

### Conditional classes
```javascript
element.classList.toggle('is-active', isActive)
```

### Event handling
```javascript
container.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
  const button = event.target.closest('[data-action="submit"]')
  if (!button) return
  handleSubmit(event)
})
```

## State Management (without frameworks)
- Local state: variables within module closure
- Cross-module communication: Custom Events (`new CustomEvent(...)`) or pub/sub module
- Shareable UI state: URL search params or hash
- Persist only non-sensitive data in `sessionStorage`; never store tokens in `localStorage`

## Data Fetching
- Use `fetch()` with explicit error handling (check `response.ok`)
- `AbortController` for cancellable requests
- Validate response shape before use; handle loading/error/empty states in UI
- Client-side validation is UX only — always validate on server too
- Never empty `catch` blocks; network failures must surface in UI state
- Error messages linked via `aria-describedby`

## Styling
- CSS in co-located `.css` files (methodology pending — update when decided)
- CSS custom properties for design tokens (`:root { --spacing-md: 1rem; }`)
- Mobile-first media queries
- Avoid inline styles except dynamically computed values

## Accessibility
- Keyboard navigable interactive elements (native `<button>`, `<a href>`)
- Visible focus styles (`:focus-visible`)
- Sufficient color contrast; don't rely on color alone
- Announce dynamic changes with `aria-live` regions when needed
- Error messages linked via `aria-describedby`

## Testing
- New features ship with a co-located `*.test.js`
- Cover the happy path and at least one validation or network error case

## Performance
- Defer non-critical JS (`<script type="module" defer>`)
- Lazy-load images (`loading="lazy"`)
- Avoid layout thrashing (batch DOM operations)
- No premature optimization; profile before optimizing
